    "4": {
      "uid": 4,
      "key": [
        "Sandrone",
        "Marionette",
        "tea party",
        "Alain's home"
      ],
      "keysecondary": [],
      "comment": "Mary-Ann: Sandrone tea party",
      "content": "In Ann, Mary-Ann, and Marionette (6.7), Mary-Ann and Ann meet Sandrone after seeing her portrait on a Fontinalia poster. Mary-Ann says that had they woken sooner they might have visited Alain. She praises the garden, jokes that Alain never decorated a room, and asks if Sandrone resents being made in the human's image. Sandrone says Alain insisted she be her own person. Mary-Ann envies her contentment and suggests more gatherings.",
